<title>ZIMBABWE: TABLE - Barclays lifts half yr shr, div.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Barclays lifts half yr shr, div.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half-yr ended June 30, 1997</p>
<p>	     (million Zimbabwe dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		     81.8	vs	60.4</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		     25.0	vs	20.0</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit	     195.8	vs     153.0</p>
<p>    Taxation			78.8	vs	67.1</p>
<p>    After-tax profit	   117.0	vs	86.0</p>
<p>    Total income		 482.9	vs     364.2</p>
<p>Div payable: September 8</p>
<p>On register: August 29.</p>
<p>Full name: Barclays Bank of Zimbabwe Limited.</p>
<p>Note:- The group said with the continued deregulation of the banking industry in the country it expected the level of competition to heighten and so was restructuring its network to make its operations more focused. It said it would give more emphasis to its main sectoral thrusts in personal/retail banking, corporate banking, agricultural finance, investment banking and asset management.</p>
<p>It said it still anticipated real growth in earnings for the second half of the year although heavy exit and restructuring costs would feature as extraordinary items in the accounts.</p>
<p>-- Harare newsroom: +263-4 72 52 27/8/9</p>
